--TEST--
Core\Ldap::connect with a granted name that no `[ldap.<name>]` block sets up throws `RuntimeError` naming the block, and the grant alone opens nothing — `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `ldap.connect` grants `corp`, but `nvs.toml` has no `[ldap.corp]` block.
try {
    var $corp = Core\Ldap::connect("corp");
    echo "opened corp", "\n";
} catch (Core\Ldap\LdapError $failed) {
    echo "not reached: ", $failed->message, "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.ldap]
connect = ["corp"]

[ldap.staff]
url = "ldaps://127.0.0.1:1"
--EXPECT--
Core\Ldap::connect: nothing sets `[ldap.corp]` up, so the name resolves to no block
